condition_name: Sjogren's Syndrome
condition_slug: sjogrens-syndrome
source: NSTG 2022
introduction: ""
clinical_features[2]:
  - type: Primary
    features[2]: Dryness of the eyes,Dryness of the mouth
  - type: Secondary
    features[2]: Dryness associated with rheumatoid arthritis,Dryness associated with other connective tissue disease
investigations[0]:
treatment:
  goals[0]:
  non_drug[7]: Sipping water frequently all day long,Letting ice melt in the mouth,Restricting caffeine intake,"Avoiding mouth rinses, drinks, and medications containing alcohol",Avoiding tobacco products,Humidifying the sleeping area,Coating the lips
  drug[3]: Sodium carboxymethylcellulose 0.5% aqueous solution (OTC); Disp. 8 floz,Saliva substitutes,"Saliva stimulants such as sugar-free gum, candy, or mints"
  adverse_reactions_and_cautions[1]: Patients should be cautioned against using products that contain sugar or have a low pH.
